From k149. k149 caps run_* and logs replies at 96 KiB (toolReplyBytes, about what Claude Code takes from one tool by default), but the read_file tool allows up to 256 KiB per call. Done when read_file's per-call maximum and its default agree with the reply cap (or the difference is argued in the tool description), with a test. Lane: unreagent-worker; after k149 lands (cmd/launcher/filetools.go, helpers.go).

Decision 2026-11-21 (main agent): read_file's per-call maximum and its default follow toolReplyBytes (48 KiB) including the reply framing, and the tool description takes the number from the constant. Bundled with k175 in one worker.

Worker result (tree commit-ready, not committed; bundled with k175).

Choice: readFileLimit = toolReplyBytes - 1<<10 = 48128 bytes (47 KiB), a const in cmd/launcher/filetools.go. The longest possible trailer, with int64-max values, is 113 bytes. I picked a whole KiB below the cap over the exact 49039 so the description reads in KiB. The description and the limit schema are built from readFileLimit with fmt.Sprintf: "At most 47 KiB per call", "offset=-48128 is the last 47 KiB", "default and maximum 48128". Paging is unchanged: the trailer "continue with offset=Y". A larger limit is still clamped, as before. A reply is at most 49152 bytes; an invalid byte becomes one U+FFFD character in the JSON, so characters stay at or below bytes.

Test: TestReadFileReplyFitsTheCap checks three things: the bound with the int64-max trailer; that the limit schema names 48128; and that a 250,000-byte file with 3-byte runes, read by following the trailer offsets (default limit and limit=10 MiB), comes back in 6 calls, each reply at most 49152 bytes, joining to the file. It is red with readFileLimit back at 256 KiB (go test -overlay). Three existing tests pinned 256 KiB; their claims are kept and only the numbers change: TestReadFileLargeFileReturnsHeadWithTotal, TestReadFileNegativeOffsetReadsTail (-65536 becomes -48128, the description example), and TestReadFileLimitIsClampedTo256KiB renamed TestReadFileLimitIsClampedTo47KiB.

Docs, not edited. Note: an offset of -65536 now returns the 47 KiB starting 64 KiB before the end, not the end of the log. For unreagent-skill-author: skills/unreagent-files/SKILL.md:165 (256 KiB), 174 (-65536 / 64 KiB), 177 (262144 / 256 KiB), 224 (example offset -65536), 230 (-262144), 301 (262144); skills/unreagent-iterate/SKILL.md:319-321 (256 KiB, -65536 / 64 KiB). For unreagent-doc-writer: README.md:1134 (offset=-65536 is the last 64 KiB; limit capped at 256 KiB).

